{%- comment -%}
  Jointwell v5 chrome, bottom half. Shared by the landing page, the advice
  pages, the policies and the app-proxy tracking page, so the whole site
  ends the same way. Styled by assets/jw-v5.css.

  Parameters, all optional:
    company_number      printed in the disclosure line. Companies Act 2006
                        s.82 requires it on a UK trading website.
    registered_address  the same.
    phone, email        contact lines. With no phone the line is dropped
                        rather than filled with a placeholder.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Every value falls back to theme settings, so a page that renders this
    with no parameters at all — the policies, the blog, the 404 — still
    prints the real contact details rather than nothing.
  endcomment
  assign jwf_phone = phone | default: settings.jw_support_phone
  assign jwf_email = email | default: settings.jw_support_email | default: 'support@velagoods.co.uk'
  assign jwf_company = company_number | default: settings.jw_company_number
  assign jwf_address = registered_address | default: settings.jw_registered_address
  assign jwf_year = 'now' | date: '%Y'

  comment
    The advice blog. The design file linked /blogs/advice; this store's blog
    is /blogs/journal, and the link 404'd. Resolve it rather than hardcode
    either one, and drop the link entirely if there is no blog at all — a
    footer link to a 404 is worse than one fewer footer link.
  endcomment
  assign jwf_blog = blogs.advice
  if jwf_blog == blank or jwf_blog.handle == blank
    assign jwf_blog = blogs.journal
  endif
  if jwf_blog == blank or jwf_blog.handle == blank
    for b in blogs
      assign jwf_blog = b
      break
    endfor
  endif
-%}

<footer>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="foot">
      <div class="foot-legal">
        <strong style="color:var(--on-deep);font-size:var(--t-base)">Jointwell</strong><br><br>
        Jointwell is a heat and massage device for the comfort and relaxation of stiff, tired knees, shoulders and elbows. It is not a medical treatment and does not cure, treat or prevent any disease or condition, including arthritis.<br><br>
        UK support by email{% if jwf_phone != blank %} and phone{% endif %}, 2-year warranty on every wrap, 90-day trial with return postage paid.<br><br>
        <a href="mailto:{{ jwf_email }}">{{ jwf_email }}</a><br>
        {%- if jwf_phone != blank -%}
          <a href="tel:{{ jwf_phone | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' }}">{{ jwf_phone }}</a>, 9am to 5pm weekdays
        {%- else -%}
          We answer email 9am to 5pm weekdays
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      <nav>
        {%- if jwf_blog.handle != blank %}<a href="{{ routes.root_url }}blogs/{{ jwf_blog.handle }}">Advice</a>{% endif -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/track-my-order">Track my order</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/returns-policy">Returns</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/shipping-policy">Shipping</a>
        {%- if shop.terms_of_service != blank %}<a href="{{ shop.terms_of_service.url }}">Terms</a>{% endif -%}
        {%- if shop.privacy_policy != blank %}<a href="{{ shop.privacy_policy.url }}">Privacy</a>{% endif -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
    <div class="disc">
      {%- comment -%}
        v4 had no company number and no address. UK buyers in this bracket
        look for both, and s.82 requires them. Until they are set this
        stays a [data-mock] placeholder, which the stylesheet hides on the
        live site and the launch guard shouts about in the console.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if jwf_company != blank -%}
        Vela Goods Ltd, company no. {{ jwf_company }}, registered in England and Wales.{% if jwf_address != blank %} {{ jwf_address }}{% endif %}<br><br>
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="todo" data-mock style="color:var(--ink-2)">Vela Goods Ltd, company no. [XXXXXXXX], registered in England and Wales. [Registered address].</span><br><br>
      {%- endif -%}
      Your right to cancel: under the Consumer Contracts Regulations 2013 you can cancel any order within 14 days of delivery for any reason. Our 90-day trial extends that, and we pay the return postage. Nothing here affects your statutory rights.<br><br>
      If you have diabetes, circulation problems or reduced skin sensation, check with your GP before using any heat product.<br><br>
      &copy; {{ jwf_year }} Jointwell is a trading name of Vela Goods Ltd
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
